pi-hashline-edit-pro — vendored bundled extension
=================================================

Upstream package : pi-hashline-edit-pro 5.1.0 (MIT)
Upstream author  : RimuruW and Yugimob (https://github.com/YuGiMob/pi-hashline-edit-pro)
License          : MIT — see LICENSE (copied verbatim from upstream)

This directory is OMA's bundled copy of the pi-hashline-edit-pro extension:

  upstream/        exact npm tarball content of pi-hashline-edit-pro@5.1.0,
                   unmodified — the integrity-pinned source snapshot. The
                   tarball's whole tree matches the source commit named in
                   manifest.json byte-for-byte.
  upstream-tests/  the upstream test tree from the source commit named in
                   manifest.json (the npm tarball does not ship tests);
                   vendored so OMA's ported boundary tests can cite and
                   re-derive upstream's fixtures. Not wired into npm test —
                   upstream's tests need vitest and the ../src layout.
  node_modules/    the pinned runtime dependency closure (diff, file-type,
                   xxhash-wasm and their transitive deps), byte-exact to the
                   npm tarballs recorded in manifest.json — kept separate
                   from anything a user-installed Pi package would resolve.
  runtime/         tsc-compiled JavaScript + declarations of upstream's
                   src/ modules, generated by scripts/vendor-pi-hashline.mjs
                   from upstream/src with upstream's own compiler options,
                   a mechanical ESM specifier rewrite, and OMA's declared
                   divergence splices (the contained read opener and the
                   contained commit channel — see generated.divergences in
                   manifest.json). Generated, hash-pinned input — not
                   authored OMA code. Upstream's entry (index.ts) and the
                   excluded feature modules (copy-move, grep, glob,
                   config-ui, auto-read-all) are vendored for provenance
                   but are never compiled or loaded: OMA registers its own
                   tool adapter (src/extension/hashline-tools.ts), which
                   keeps workspace, quota and mutation authority in OMA.
  manifest.json    generated bundle manifest: per-file SHA-256, byte
                   counts and a deterministic whole-bundle digest, plus
                   the upstream name/version/commit, npm tarball
                   integrity/shasum metadata and the pinned dependency
                   closure.

No part of this bundle is fetched, installed or cloned at run time.
